  "project_description": "Back to top \n\n Summary \n Applies a configurable image style when uploading image files on the website.\n\n This can be very handy when you are working with an optimize pipeline on your image style.\n\nWhen a content editor then adds a big file, the original file will already go through a process of optimisation (typically the width will be reduced - by default an upload image style is added of 2000px width).\n\n Back to top \n\n How to configure \n After installing and enabling the module, go to: /admin/config/media/image_style_on_upload\n\nSelect an image style and configure the mime types of the files that you wish to alter:\n\n \n\n Save and export configuration...\n\n That's all there is to it!\n\n Back to top",
